      "writtenOn": "2018-09-19T00:34:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question, it can call task_reset() on itself safely iff, wait\u003d0 \u0026\u0026 resets are disabled when it calls task_reset()\n\nI had been thinking (though I realise I failed to document this) that we wouldn\u0027t support tasks resetting themselves, as I wasn\u0027t sure there was much of a use case for this (eg they could achieve the same result using some normal logic). \n\nThat said, it should be very simple to support this - happy to go ahead and do that if you think it\u0027s useful",
      "parentUuid": "76a6482e_9b86fe0d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 280,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 281,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "0251e7f56c39bff7001c756f3e1750cbcc6f3673",
